body:
Hm...good sleuthing. Unfortunately, the only work-around I can think of is to store the window's scroll position and scroll back to it after calling `.select()`. Something like:

```ts
const [x, y] = [window.pageXOffset, window.pageYOffset];
this.fakeElem.select();
window.scrollTo(x, y);
```

But I am a little wary of adding such a hack 🤔
